            <div xml:id="d998">

                <pb facs="1248" n="1238" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg1238"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12–1247: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-12-23T15:00:00-05:00">December 23,
                            1947—3 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1558. Not now possible give any definite info re Blandford (Embtel 2381 Dec 12)
                    and civilian advisory group pending agreement by Dept and concerned Govt
                    agencies on China aid program now being prepared for presentation Congress. You
                    may in your discretion tell Gimo matter being studied by Dept and other Govt
                    agencies but no final decision yet reached.</p>
                <p>As regards inquiry re subject matter para 2 of Reftel Dept assumes you have by
                    now reed memo of conversation betw Sec and Amb Koo Nov 13 forwarded by
                    pouch.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
